# FUZZ SEEDS ARE BINARY, and a tool that reads a commit's diff as text
# has to be told so.
#
# A pinned seed is an arbitrary byte string. Where it happens to hold no
# NUL, git guesses TEXT and prints its bytes into a diff, and those bytes
# are not valid UTF-8: a tool that read `git diff-tree -p` in text mode
# died on the first such seed (22 Sep 2026, `read_seam`'s
# `encrypted-split-crc32`). Marking the seed
# trees binary makes git print "Binary files differ" instead, which every
# tool here can read, and it is what these files ARE.
fuzz/seeds/** binary
crates/rarkit/fuzz/seeds/** binary
# The notes that live among the seeds are text. Without these two lines
# the globs above make them binary too, and a diff of a change to one
# shows nothing to review.
fuzz/seeds/**/README.md -binary text
crates/rarkit/fuzz/seeds/**/README.md -binary text

# THE GATE TEXT'S WORD LIST IS LINE FEEDS ONLY. The test data crate takes
# it in at build time and pins a digest of the text made from it; the
# reading drops a carriage return, but the file is kept the same bytes on
# every checkout all the same.
crates/rarkit-testdata/src/source_words.txt text eol=lf
